# Cursor Rules for AutoAgent

## Drevvy sources of truth

This product is Drevvy (repo still uses the AutoAgent name). Two documents are the strategic source of truth. Read them before changing MarketCheck, MCP/API inventory search, dealer workflow, monetization, events, or data architecture. If older AutoAgent docs conflict, these files win unless a newer written decision explicitly overrides them.

- `docs/drevvy/DREVVY_CONTEXT.md` — product vision, business model, MarketCheck relationship, consumer/dealer experience, legal guardrails
- `docs/drevvy/DREVVY_DATA_ARCHITECTURE.md` — target data layers, MarketCheck MCP/API vs feed usage, event taxonomy, IDs, search/ranking, engineering rules

Index: `docs/drevvy/README.md`

Preserve the product direction in those documents. MarketCheck is the upstream inventory/data provider; Drevvy owns search, ranking, the consumer relationship, dealer workflow, offers, analytics, and transaction intelligence.

## Markdown Documentation

When creating new markdown files, run the documentation updater to keep the summary current:

```bash
pnpm update-docs
```

Or use watch mode to automatically update:

```bash
pnpm watch-docs
```

This will automatically analyze and add new markdown files to `MARKDOWN_FILES_SUMMARY.md`.

See `scripts/README_MARKDOWN_UPDATER.md` for details.

